{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left| \\,\\frac{{{a}_{n+1}}}{{{a}_{n}}} \\,\\right|=\\dfrac{25}{16}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]\n","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left| \\,\\frac{{{a}_{n+1}}}{{{a}_{n}}} \\,\\right|\u0026=\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{ (n+1)\\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)^{2(n+1)+1} }{ n \\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)^{2n+1}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026\\displaystyle=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{ (n+1)\\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)^{2n+3} }{ n \\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)^{2n+1}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026\\displaystyle=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{(n+1)\\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)^2}{n}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\left(\\dfrac{5}{4}\\right)^2\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{25}{16}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire process.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Since the limit, $\\dfrac{25}{16}$, is greater than $1$, the ratio rest tells us that the series diverges.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$a_n={n\\left(\\dfrac{5}{4}\\right)^{2n+1}}$\n\n**1) Find $\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left| \\dfrac{a_{n+1}}{a_n} \\right|$.**\n\n$\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left|\\, \\frac{{{a}_{n+1}}}{{{a}_{n}}} \\,\\right|=$ [[☃ input-number 1]]\n\n**2) Based on your answer, what does the ratio test say about $S=\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n$?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"input-number 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerType":"number","inexact":false,"maxError":0.1,"simplify":"required","size":"normal","value":1.5625},"static":false,"type":"input-number","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}},"radio 1":